{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI NOTE ON PATCH SET 3 — the Verified -1 currently visible on BOTH changes is a COPIED-FORWARD VOTE,\nnot a PS3 result. Do not act on it and do not recheck yet.\n\nEVIDENCE: the two PS3 runs were dispatched at 23:58:18Z and 23:58:20Z and are still QUEUED, so\nneither has cast a vote. A vote that exists before its run concludes cannot have come from that run.\nA rebase is a trivial change by Gerrit's copy conditions, so the PS2 -1 (which was itself caused by\nthe pre-fix pip-audit block) was carried across.\n\nA RISK I CREATED AND AM WATCHING: I pushed both changes in a single push, which dispatched the two\nruns TWO SECONDS APART — exactly the window in which gerrit-verify.yaml's concurrency group fails to\nisolate per change under load (see the CI-infrastructure comment above). If one cancels the other, the\nsymptom is a Verified -1 from a run whose build-and-test job is SKIPPED, with no test having executed.\nTHE REMEDY IF THAT HAPPENS IS TO RECHECK ONE CHANGE AT A TIME, not both — rechecking a stacked pair in\nthe same breath reproduces the cancellation, and can also cancel an unrelated agent's in-flight run.\n\nHOW TO TELL A REAL FAILURE FROM THE ARTIFACT: check whether build-and-test actually RAN\n(gh run view <id> --repo navapbc/rebar --json jobs). Do NOT diagnose from log text — the workflow log\nechoes its own ::error:: lines and has misdirected readers repeatedly in this session.\n\nEXPECTED OUTCOME once a PS3 run really executes: pip-audit passes, because the rebased base\n(31844d5f9fb) contains the click override. That was the only outstanding failure after PS2 fixed the\ndocs/env-vars.md drift."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785715228192712001,"uuid":"b573b2a3-8e25-46dd-8ab4-07a97402d815"}